        "student_prefix_sha256": "94b83a9f2bf249f2dad40f3783c6df8bd368d2a52ef4e8de4e68882d54d78c7f",
        "target": "First, I calculate the total number of words Jenny needs to read. The first book has 200 words, the second has 400 words, and the third has 300 words. So, the total is 200 + 400 + 300 = 900 words.\n\nNext, I determine how many hours she needs to read all 900 words. Since she reads 100 words per hour, she needs 900 / 100 = 9 hours.\n\nTo find out how many minutes per day she should spend reading, I convert the total hours into minutes. 9 hours is 9 * 60 = 540 minutes.\n\nSince she has 10 days to read, I divide the total minutes by the number of days: 540 / 10 = 54 minutes per day.\n\nFINAL: 54",
