    "gold": "26",
    "question": "Mobius is the fastest mule in Italy.  She can run at a top speed of 13 miles per hour when she is without any load to carry, and she can travel at 11 miles per hour as her top speed when she carries a typical load.  If she travels the 143 miles from Florence, Italy to Rome, Italy at top speed while carrying a typical load, then returns to Florence at her usual top speed without carrying a load, how long, in hours, will the trip take if she takes two 30-minute rest stops during each half of the trip?",
    "question_sha256": "cef3ead81ff8b03fc1e48e0d45c68b50b4959f86e57d7a7a460dc1e95c1a5de9",
    "responses": [
      {
        "key": "gsm8k-train-6849:rich",
        "raw_call_sha256": "4280faa1bc3383e3d7319f529e53bcddadc3b235a479804f14cefb9b7f530e4e",
        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "Mobius is the fastest mule in Italy.  She can run at a top speed of 13 miles per hour when she is without any load to carry, and she can travel at 11 miles per hour as her top speed when she carries a typical load.  If she travels the 143 miles from Florence, Italy to Rome, Italy at top speed while carrying a typical load, then returns to Florence at her usual top speed without carrying a load, how long, in hours, will the trip take if she takes two 30-minute rest stops during each half of the trip?",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "56c7bd786b8ca5f5cdc223bfde194b54f0bbb37afccfba17420cacb5f8f76730",
        "target": "Given:\n- Mobius' top speed with load: 11 miles per hour\n- Mobius' top speed without load: 13 miles per hour\n- Distance between Florence and Rome: 143 miles\n- Rest stops: 2 at 30 minutes each per half of the trip\n\nFirst, calculate the time to travel from Florence to Rome with a load:\n- Time = Distance / Speed = 143 miles / 11 mph = 13 hours\n\nNext, calculate the time to travel from Rome to Florence without a load:\n- Time = Distance / Speed = 143 miles / 13 mph = 11 hours\n\nTotal travel time without rest stops:\n- 13 hours + 11 hours = 24 hours\n\nNow, calculate the rest time:\n- 2 rest stops at 30 minutes each = 1 hour of rest per half of the trip\n- Total rest time = 1 hour (Florence to Rome) + 1 hour (Rome to Florence) = 2 hours\n\nTotal trip time including rest stops:\n- 24 hours + 2 hours = 26 hours\n\nFINAL: 26",
        "target_sha256": "5ef3ea2c49f7803fe652df87b28db380969dea29ba3fbb43570926bfe5c105f8"
