        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the key quantities and the unknown:\n- Mobius' top speed with load: 11 miles per hour\n- Mobius' top speed without load: 13 miles per hour\n- Distance between Florence and Rome: 143 miles\n- Rest stops: 2 at 30 minutes each per half of the trip\n\nThe unknown is the total time for the round trip, including rest stops.\n\nFirst, I calculated the time to travel from Florence to Rome with a load:\n- Time = Distance / Speed = 143 miles / 11 mph = 13 hours\n\nNext, I calculated the time to travel from Rome to Florence without a load:\n- Time = Distance / Speed = 143 miles / 13 mph = 11 hours\n\nAdding these times together gave the total travel time without rest stops:\n- 13 hours + 11 hours = 24 hours\n\nThen, I calculated the total rest time:\n- 2 rest stops at 30 minutes each = 1 hour of rest per half of the trip\n- Total rest time = 1 hour (Florence to Rome) + 1 hour (Rome to Florence) = 2 hours\n\nAdding the rest time to the travel time gave the total trip time:\n- 24 hours + 2 hours = 26 hours\n\nTo verify, I checked the arithmetic and the logic of the operations:\n- 143 / 11 = 13\n- 143 / 13 = 11\n- 13 + 11 = 24\n- 24 + 2 = 26\n\nThe operations and their results align with the problem statement, confirming the total trip time.\n\nFINAL: 26",
